Original commit body from fd22fc1:

Use semantic similarity to extract project descriptions from READMEs:
- Compare each line against probe embeddings of known project mission statements
- Sliding window approach finds best consecutive description lines
- Quality-based stopping: stop when similarity score drops 10%+
- Falls back to heuristic parsing if embeddings unavailable

This fixes the bug where heuristic extraction picked code snippets
(e.g., litellm's Python import) instead of actual descriptions.
